{title: 147 - Christ Upon the Mountain Peak}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #147 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 147}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Christ [Bb]upon [F]the [Am]mountain peak
[Gm]Stands alone [Bb]in [C]glory [Dm]blazing;
[F]Let [Gm/Bb]us, [F]if [Gm]we [F]dare to [C/G]speak,
[Gm]With [C]the saints and [Bb]angels [F]praise [Bb]Him:
[Eb]Alleluia, [F]Alleluia, [Am]Alleluia.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Trembling [Gm]at [F]His [Am]feet [Bb]we [Am/C]saw
[Gm]Moses [F/A]and [Bb]Elijah [Dm]speaking;
[F]All [Gm/Bb]the [F]prophets and the [C/G]law
[Gm]Shout [C]thro'them their [Bb]joyful [F]greeting:
[Eb]Alleluia, [F]Alleluia, [Am]Alleluia.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Swift [Bb]the [Gm]cloud [F]of [Am]glory came,
[Gm]God proclaiming [C]in the [Dm]thunder
[F]Jesus as [Gm]His [F]Son by [C/G]name;
[Gm]Nations [C]cry aloud in [F]wonder!
[Eb]Alleluia, [F]Alleluia, [Am]Alleluia.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]This [Bb]is [Gm]God's [C7/G]beloved [Am/C]Son:
[Gm]Law and [F/A]prophets [C]fade before [Gm]Him;
[F]First [Gm/Bb]and [F]last, [Gm]the [F]only [C/G]One,
[Gm]Let [C]creation now [Bb]adore [F]Him.
[Eb]Alleluia, [F]Alleluia, [Am]Alleluia.
{end_of_verse}
